# Env — no `.env*` template of any shape is tracked (per CONTRIBUTING.md §6). Variable names live
# in each app's README; real values live in the developer's local working file (.env.local for
# Vite, .env for Django) and in the deployment provider's secret store. The allowlist is empty by
# design — a stray `.env.example` or `.env.local.example` will not slip back in.
.env
.env.*

